WEBVTT

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.350
I'm exhausted...

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.450
Water...

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.640
Today's practice was extra tough, wasn't it?

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.990
The captain was pumped.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.400
Well, this <i>is</i> the third-years' last summer.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.620
Isn't the Hanazono 
tournament in the winter?

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.080
What about exams?

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.830
I can't imagine the captain 
studying for entrance exams.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.790
Coach Komori's pumped, too.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.840
He could at least treat us
to meals sometimes.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.620
Isn't that what coaches are supposed to do?

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.390
He took us to a restaurant after our 
training camp at school that one time.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.400
That place was good.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.470
Maybe he'll take us there again.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.830
Should we ask him?

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.480
No way! He's terrifying!

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.330
Okay, whoever loses 
goes and asks him.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.190
Rock, paper, scissors...

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.400
Coach just left.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.400
What?

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:03.990
Yu-chan.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.820
Long time, no see.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.670
Shingo, I've been waitin' 
for you, you bastard.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.280
<b>Restaurant Nagabe</b>

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.280
Welcome!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.780
Komo-san! Tomie-san!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.290
Hey, Nagata. Long time, no see.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.800
<b>Episode 14    X Day</b>

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.560
This is your place, huh?

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.080
What are you doing in a wheelchair?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.470
I had surgery on my foot the other day.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.570
I can still putter about the house, though.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:14.420
Who is it?

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.390
Komo-san and Tomie Yujiro-san!

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.900
They were two years above me 
on the college rugby team.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.680
Make them something good.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.430
Say what?

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.170
Hey! We have that thing we made this morning!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.070
I can't believe you're coaching 
a high school team, Shingo.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.340
Huh? What was it?

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.890
Where did I put it? Where is it? Over here?

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.270
Surprising, isn't it?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.200
You've always liked kids,
so I can understand you doing it.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.220
What are you doing?

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:35.690
Is it in there?

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.720
You're in the way! Move! Move!

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.720
But... But!

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.160
How long have you been coaching?

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.680
Sheesh!

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.570
I've been coaching for over 20 years now.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.520
Middle school, high school...

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.380
I've coached college and 
grade school teams, too.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.460
They're so cute.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.460
It's like they're playing at it.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.030
But they put their all into it.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.030
As a man who once played 
for the national team,

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:06.470
high school teams must look like 
they're just messing around, right?

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.730
Sorry. I misspoke.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.810
Komo-san! Tomie-san! What are you drinking?

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.230
I'd like some warm sake.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.060
Honey, get him the best sake we have!

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.120
Calm down, dear!

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.940
And use the good bottle!

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.230
Who are you coaching now?

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:25.740
I know, I know!

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.940
Where is it? Here it is!

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.940
High school students.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:30.980
Calm down!

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:31.610
Just like you, I'm coaching an 
ordinary public school team.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.970
How good are their facilities?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.750
They've got a weights room.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.000
Your place doesn't have one, right?

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:40.410
Nope.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:47.150
That explains why your blog is
full of nostalgic training programs.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.780
That's right. I've been reading your blog.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:55.140
I laughed at your post 
the other day about the beach.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.460
Well, yeah.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.270
Naga, hurry up with that sake!

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.660
I've never seen this before.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.870
So this is...

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.940
What is it?

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.410
Coach Komori's blog.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.150
It's plain.

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:11.730
So very plain.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:14.660
Gion, I'm impressed you found this blog.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.800
Yeah.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.910
You're still hungry?

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.740
Huh? Where's Keta?

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.750
Sounds like you're having fun.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:33.450
Jinko seems to have some pretty good boys.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.440
I don't know about that.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.770
But they're managing
 to complete my training.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.420
I guess the team's made up of hard workers.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.020
Sounds nice.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.450
On my team, there's a big gap 
between the boys who are motivated

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.520
and those that aren't.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.250
Every team's like that.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.090
Thanks for waiting!

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.410
You don't need to run, Nagata.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.420
Here you are.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.420
Thanks.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:00.550
Here you are.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.440
Thanks.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.920
Nagata, have a drink with us.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.590
No, I can't.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.050
Enjoy yourselves.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:09.620
Bring us whatever you recommend.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.620
Yes, sir! Right away!

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.090
Cheers.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:13.810
Cheers.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.580
That's good.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:29.840
What?

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.870
Shingo, you've gone soft in your old age.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.750
Up until a few years ago, 
you used to scowl a lot more.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:45.910
The moment I saw your face today, 
I thought "wow, he's gotten softer."

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.300
You think so?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.510
Apparently, the Jinko boys are afraid of me.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:57.130
Well, it's no wonder,
considering you frown all the time.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:00.770
I can tell you've changed because 
I've known you for a long time.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.170
You were so serious when you 
were on the national team.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.710
You were always worrying 
about your performance.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:25.170
And when you found out your wife, 
Yumi-chan, couldn't have kids...

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.440
You've been through a lot.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.830
I can't blame you for having a scary face.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:42.260
I wish I'd started coaching sooner, 
instead of being weirdly stubborn about it.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.520
You're not too late.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.530
Here you are! Thank you for waiting!

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:55.140
This is pretty good, Shingo.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:56.280
Okay.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:10.800
At first, the Jinko boys were awful at rugby.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.520
But lately, they've gotten a lot better.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:20.670
They don't have any weights sets, 
but they're starting to build muscle.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:27.400
A lot of the second-years weren't very 
motivated, but these days, they are.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.430
Yeah...

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:32.830
They still can't win a game, though.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:35.480
But you played Sagami, didn't you?

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.070
There's no way you'd beat them.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:41.260
But the captain's a serious guy.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:45.830
Even after getting smashed 
by Sagami, he's still optimistic.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.710
I hope he stays on as their 
captain for a long time.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:56.430
Ensuring things like that is our job.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.310
It's a hard job.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.070
Nagata, this is good sake.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.170
Bring us two more.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:10.070
Yes, sir!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.410
Since I retired...

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:18.040
I thought I'd have nothing to do.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:23.290
I started writing a blog and 
said I'd start coaching.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:27.460
That's when I got an offer
from some amusingly dumb kid.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:29.270
Passing the time...

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:33.050
I was supposed to just be passing the time.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.240
But it's so much fun.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.310
I feel like I have a bunch of kids now.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.700
I don't think I'll ever 
want to play rugby again...

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:10.880
But I wanted to teach my kids to play.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.670
Have you introduced them to Yumi-chan?

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.860
No, not yet.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.930
She wants to meet them.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.280
But that makes me uncomfortable.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.570
You can't keep all the fun to yourself.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:28.150
I know, I know.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:32.260
And smile for them a little more,
like you used to.

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.230
No chance.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.540
Thanks for the food, Nagata.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.370
It was good. Think I could 
come back again sometime?

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.590
O-Of course!

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.700
We should get more of the college 
gang together next time!

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.370
I'll reach out to them!

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:50.570
Good idea.

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:53.250
Thanks. Get in touch with me anytime.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.640
Take care!

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.740
Thank you!

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.260
Sorry, Yu-chan.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:07.140
I invited you out so I could 
ask you about coaching,

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.590
but we talked about me the whole time.

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:12.600
It's fine. I had fun.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:19.700
Oh, just one last thing...

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.950
Huh?

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:26.580
X Day's coming up before summer break.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:32.010
Bye, Shingo. See you later.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.000
<b>Shingo and Yu-chan Back Then</b>

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.000
Strum
Strum

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:37.000
<b>Yu-chan, 
shut up!!</b>

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.000
<b>My
hair
 is...</b>

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.010
<b>WHACK</b>

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.010
<b>Second-year       First Semester
    Final Exam         Math II</b>

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:43.010
<b>Class 2-6      Number 28     Noka Taihei</b>

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:51.340
So bright.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:54.620
So hot.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:59.190
Yoshida-sensei, a student's asking for you.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.450
Coming.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:08.450
Um...

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:11.350
I'm Keta, a first-year on the rugby team.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.830
Oh, the rugby team.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:17.560
<i>Has this guy always been on the team?</i>

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.090
What do you want?

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.970
Takuya-kun, I'm hungry!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.560
That's not my problem.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.830
Let's go to practice.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:31.600
Sekizan.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.550
Yoshida-sensei, what—

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:38.980
Keta's... quit the team.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.490
<b>Club Resignation</b>

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.490
Keta Yuto

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:46.950
A lot of guys quit sports teams
before summer break.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:50.500
Sekizan!

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:07.860
<i>X Day's coming up before summer break.</i>

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.740
<i>X Day...</i>

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:12.750
<i>So this is what he meant.</i>

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:20.480
Keta!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.770
C-Captain...

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:29.450
Keta...

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.950
Y-You're quitting?

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:36.750
Oh, uh...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.430
Why?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.750
Was practice too hard?

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:50.890
I-It's hard for me, too.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:56.620
L-Lately, you've gotten better 
at handling the ball.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:14:02.510
W-We've been talking about 
how you'd make a good lock.

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:07.290
Why don't you keep at it 
for just a little longer?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:14.120
Lately, I...

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:20.130
I-I haven't been able to eat.

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:23.050
I throw everything up.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:30.660
I'm so tired every day, I have no appetite.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:38.520
Practice every day is just so hard.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:44.410
My parents have been telling me
to quit the team.

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:46.330
But...

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:52.980
everyone on the team is so fun to be around.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:59.270
They'd play with me even if 
we'd never really talked before.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:00.460
It was fun.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:07.520
Captain, I really like you, too.

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:10.820
You're amazing. Y-You're cool.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:17.700
I'll probably... always look up to you.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.210
It's not that I don't like the team anymore.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:24.500
Please, just know that.

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:30.460
W-We could change how we do things—

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.450
It's my fault!

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:37.790
Huh? Keta's not coming.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.330
He was at school.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.820
What? Have the first-years 
finally started skipping?

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:45.570
Keta, huh? He doesn't have much stamina.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:48.580
I've never really talked to him.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.640
Me neither.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.420
Come to think of it, where's the captain?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:57.790
He said he'd be a little late and 
to start practice without him.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.210
I understand.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.970
Thanks for giving us your best
for three months.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:12.990
But Keta, promise me this...

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.610
We'll definitely make it to Hanazono.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:19.870
So you'd better come cheer us on.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:26.330
Yes, sir.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:06.880
Oh, right. Arukimizu Beach is 
a place to swim and have fun.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:14.170
I thought it was going to be 
the training spot from hell.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.610
I don't want to go there for a while.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.640
We'll be spending our entire 
summer vacation on the field.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.890
Gather round!

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:26.580
Starting August 10th,
we're attending a five-day,

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:28.910
four-night training camp in Sugadaira.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:31.270
You've found someplace for us to stay, right?

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:35.000
Yes, sir. We always make 
reservations at the same place.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.000
The old man looks like 
some kind of gang leader.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.020
Gion-kun...

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:38.280
What's Sugadaira?

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:44.670
It's a place in Nagano where the nation's 
student rugby teams hold a training camp.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.970
It has over a hundred fields,

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:51.920
and teams from all over 
play each other all day, every day.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:55.710
Let's play as many games as 
we can over those five days.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:59.050
We have a little more than two weeks 
before the training camp starts.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:02.440
Prepare yourselves to play 
against teams from around the nation.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:03.560
You got that?

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:10.060
Tree Trunk, help me practice again today.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.910
What? Okay...

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.700
I'm going to knock down Ryoin's giant.

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:19.830
You mean Zanba-san, right? 
The guy with the scary face...

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:23.030
But I'm not sure I can help you with that.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:26.580
Our weights are probably totally different.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.580
Then, get fatter.

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.420
That's crazy! Ow!

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:37.420
Try tackling me, Gion.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.440
You sure?

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:47.180
I'll flip you on your back again.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.190
Wrong!

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:57.690
I told you before!

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:00.510
Don't charge straight into their stomachs!

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:04.950
Don't forget that it's easy to 
deflect a tackle to the stomach!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.370
Wrong!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.160
You're starting too low!

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.380
You'll just get knocked down
by their stiff-arm fend!

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:16.630
Don't charge in recklessly!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:21.260
If you want to get stronger, 
abandon your recklessness!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.640
Focus on the minutiae of your technique!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.730
Let's keep practicing!

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.440
I'm exhausted!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.800
The captain was scary today.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:40.950
Do you think it's because of Keta?

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:45.790
Sekizan's not here.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.530
Yeah, he went running.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:52.290
He doesn't...

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:58.760
...think it's all his fault, does he?

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:13.970
I thought I told you that resting is
 an important part of training, Captain.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.320
I can't sit around and do nothing.

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:22.260
You told Short Stuff to stop being reckless,

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:26.070
but you're just as reckless as ever yourself.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:27.390
Sorry.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:30.620
This is all I know how to do.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.930
But the first-years and 
second-years are different.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:38.730
They have someone to show them the right way!

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:45.400
Training recklessly hasn't 
made me stronger.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:50.470
I couldn't even stop a teammate
from quitting!

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:55.260
What we've been doing isn't good enough.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:59.450
Our technique isn't... nor are our tactics...

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.910
You don't have to give up on being reckless.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:09.290
Your recklessness is what 
has got you to this point.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:13.910
You don't need to get rid of it.

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:20.750
I like your recklessness.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:23.700
It's not that I don't like the team anymore.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.010
Please, just know that.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.700
And don't worry.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.650
I know we'll win the next one.

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:40.280
Keep doing what you're doing.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:45.780
If I ever think you're about to 
make a mistake, I'll correct you.

00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:48.780
Don't try to do it all yourself.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:50.830
You're not alone.

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.050
<b>Ise Natsuki</b>

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.050
I'll talk to my 
brother tomorrow.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "Teammate"</b>

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.870
Next time: "Teammate!"
